WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.560
When I buy the collection or when I get
the figure it's mainly for...

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:05.260
For peace of mind,

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:10.120
and there's this whole mentality of
"if I don't have a specific figure, I cannot sleep."

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:22.260
My first collection was G.I. Joe comics
when I was 9 years old.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:25.040
I still remember this
very clearly, I had a really good friend

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:29.060
he had this issue of G.I. Joe I thought
was really good and the cover was Cobra Commander.

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:31.830
The colors really popped and then from

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:37.079
there the love for superheroes grew from
that comic collection.

00:00:37.079 --> 00:00:42.930
The tactility of a figure or a statue is
very special right so when you

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:47.520
see a character let's say for example my
favorite character, Nightcrawler,

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:52.170
looking at the image on the page and
holding it is two very different things

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:57.780
based off that feeling or and I decided
that collecting action figures fulfills

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:02.000
a deeper need for that love than
just print.

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:05.100
Hi! My name is Neal, I'm 45 years old.

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.120
and welcome to my superhero man cave

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:32.040
Oddly enough, I didn't collect action
figures to begin with.

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:33.880
My first piece was Doctor Doom.

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:36.760
The whole idea of collecting
Doctor Doom was not so much

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:40.640
about the character because I wasn't really that interested in Doctor Doom but the pose,

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:47.280
the sculpting, the whole essence of
how he looked was just incredible.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:48.480
It called out to me.

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:51.120
I could literally hear the voice inside my head saying, "You have to buy me!"

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:54.840
and at 14 years of age, you don't really have a lot of money.

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:57.560
I could still remember the shop from Siglap Center

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:00.520
and the owner was very nice so when I told the uncle,

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:05.920
"Hey I really want this, is there any way
I can do some sort of like deposit kind

00:02:05.929 --> 00:02:10.489
of thing - he's very nice when he says
okay little boy, you can just pay me $50

00:02:10.489 --> 00:02:12.769
a month I think after five months you can get it."

00:02:12.769 --> 00:02:14.720
so that's how I managed to get Doctor Doom.

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:17.240
I don't really follow the market prices

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:19.840
because when I buy the
collection or when I get the figure

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:24.760
it's mainly for peace of mind and there's this 
whole mentality of...

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:29.800
"If I dont have a specific figure, I cannot sleep."
It'll always be in my mind trying to think about

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:33.680
"okay how do I get this?", you know ," where can I go?" 
it's always a little nagging doubt

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:34.960
that keeps me awake at night.

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:37.560
Most of it are action figures are from a

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:42.680
six inch scale and most of my figures are
from the DC side are either

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:57.319
Mattel or DC Direct then for Marvel is
either Hasbro or Marvel Select

00:02:57.319 --> 00:03:02.370
Currently I have a supplier like a
personal friend of mine,

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:05.970
he is the one going to get all this action
figures so shout out to Mervin Foo that

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:08.080
gets all of my items for me.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:10.960
It's not so much a collection then it's an obsession.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:15.280
to me it's almost like a drug.
Every time I get a certain item that has been hard to find,

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:20.480
I feel this whole sense
of accomplishment.

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:25.920
In the past there were certain figures that - because of the way the company distributes it.

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:29.920
there will be rare figures that are so hard to find that even though you searched

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:35.519
all around you cannot find it, and I was
lucky enough that, back then my work

00:03:35.519 --> 00:03:39.480
allowed me to travel. Every time I travel
I will visit all the toy stores and find

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:41.880
the figures at Singapore doesn't have.

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:44.160
Currently I have everything I need to have.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:48.120
For Marvel Legends I have
every single figure produced back when

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:52.470
it was under ToyBiz in the late 90s and
moved over to Hasbro Legends.

00:03:52.470 --> 00:03:56.069
I have every single figure,
even the exclusives and the variants.

00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:59.849
During that period, some of them will
really hard to get because I think one

00:03:59.849 --> 00:04:03.810
of the waves was exclusive to like a
retailer in the U.S. that was really hard to get.

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:07.709
Even within the region you
cannot find it and this is back before the

00:04:07.709 --> 00:04:11.760
"internet days", back before Amazon...
that wave would be the Giant Man wave.

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:16.769
You've really got to search high and low to find it,
which eventually I managed to find it.

00:04:16.769 --> 00:04:21.640
I had to pay every pretty penny, the prices were at least
three to four times what would have gone at retail.

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:25.760
So the thing about collecting
is how you display them.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:28.600
Collectors are also hoarders, the only
difference between hoarders and collectors

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:33.570
are that the collectors are
able to display them in a very nice way

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:37.480
and identify where everything lies
specifically.

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:39.440
Most of the items has a

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:41.560
very special emotional connection and
memory attached to it.

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:47.000
If you point out to a specific figure, I can probably
tell you a bit more about where I was,

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:50.880
what I was doing when I purchased it. To
me story is also very important it has

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:54.760
to be correct to that characters story line.

00:04:54.800 --> 00:05:00.560
If you know the history of Ghost Rider, he rides
a motorcycle and because of his supernatural abilities,

00:05:00.760 --> 00:05:03.000
his motorcycle can go up vertical surfaces.

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:06.880
How I display the Ghost Rider figures are all
on vertical sections.

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:10.200
Spider-man is the easiest because Spider-Man swings from building to building.

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:13.330
Again, if you look at
all the stuff you see all the various

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:20.230
Spider-Mans' swinging from location to
location and I also try not to duplicate

00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:25.740
my Spider-Man in terms of the poses so
every Spider-Man has a unique pose

00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:28.240
that is identifiable to his action.

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:35.640
Todd McFarlane had a very unique, distinct style whenever he drew Spider-Man's web.

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:40.960
- I don't throw away anything so I still have twisty ties, it grew to a point where it started to get out of hand.

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:44.840
and I realized if I actually joined
all the twisty ties it looked almost

00:05:44.840 --> 00:05:47.080
identical to Todd McFarlane's web...

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:49.440
I had a really good friend back then,

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:54.680
he was like a DIY carpenter. He came in, he
suggested hey you know why don't you put it on the ceiling.

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:58.640
you can actually built
like a walkway, catwalks across.

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:04.720
Then I have all these walkways for additional
collection and additional display.

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:11.260
What I've learned is careful planning and
making sure that every figure can stand on

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:15.420
its own so that when the figures are
displayed all by itself

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:21.010
it looks natural. I tend to arrange them
by grouping, again, it's always about the story.

00:06:21.010 --> 00:06:27.820
So if we look at this level here...

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:32.320
They're all arranged according to their groups so
like the Superman group, the Batman group

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:37.720
and the Justice League, Justice Society
and the magic users and then so on and so forth.

00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:41.790
How much is it worth? About five
years ago I did a rough calculation

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:47.440
everything's worth about $150,000 (Singapore Dollars) all together

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:55.330
One statue is about $300 to $350 and I have about
maybe 400 to 500 pieces and

00:06:55.330 --> 00:06:58.990
then one action figure is about let's
see $20 to $30 and I have about two thousand.

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:06.360
Now, I think I wouldn't sell
anything because these are the stuff that I really want.

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:10.440
If there's a fire I
have probably saved myself first.

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:14.520
My rationale is money you can always make,
stuff you can always collect but health and

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:18.640
family is one thing that you can never
replace.

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:24.440
If I go head in and burn myself then I would not be able to enjoy my other collection in the future.

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:31.080
Personally yes
I feel like my life would be duller without the collection.

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:35.320
When I have like a
long day and I come here I sit down look

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:40.960
look at some of the pieces, it helps me to to
relax and gives me peace of mind so that

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:48.760
when I look at a certain range
or a certain grouping, the mind naturally slows down

00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:53.000
and any stress or problems that
I'm facing at work or home

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:58.070
sort of is able to go under the
undercurrent and then when I step out of the room,

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:02.090
I have a different frame of mind
and I can approach the challenge in a different way.

00:08:02.090 --> 00:08:07.320
Collectors need to have more interaction

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:12.520
with each other because I know a few collectors
 out there who we happen to be friends with.

00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:16.250
But I'm sure there are other
people out there that have better or

00:08:16.250 --> 00:08:19.970
different kind of collections and I'm always
trying to see whether I can meet up with them

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:25.070
because I think we share the same
passion. If you're gonna display them in

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:29.570
this kind of manner and only you see it
I think it's a bit of a shame right?

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:33.560
So for me, anyone that wants to come in
and see, I'm happy to invite them.

00:08:33.560 --> 00:08:37.640
I also feel like there are people out there that have the same kind of mind frame.

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:42.440
It'll be nice if we can have a like a
collecting community/gathering where

00:08:42.440 --> 00:08:45.600
We can we can sit down and visit each other's home.

